  "explanation": "In modern C++, template specialization and SFINAE (Substitution Failure Is Not An Error) are powerful techniques that enable compile-time type introspection and conditional compilation. They allow developers to write generic code that adapts to different types or conditions, improving code flexibility, safety, and efficiency. These features are essential for creating highly generic libraries, such as the Standard Template Library (STL), and for implementing type traits, enable_if conditions, and optimized algorithms.",
  "syntax": "template <typename T>\nstruct TypeTrait {\n    static constexpr bool value = false;\n};\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct TypeTrait<int> {\n    static constexpr bool value = true;\n};\n\n// SFINAE example with enable_if\n\ntemplate <typename T>\ntypename std::enable_if<TypeTrait<T>::value, void>::type\nfoo(T t) {\n    // Implementation for types where TypeTrait<T>::value == true\n}\n\n// Specialization for specific types\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct MyClass {\n    // General template\n};\ntemplate <>\nstruct MyClass<int> {\n    // Specialization for int\n};",
  "code_example": [
    "#include <type_traits>",
    "#include <iostream>",
    "",
    "template <typename T>",
    "struct IsInteger {",
    "    static constexpr bool value = false;",
    "};",
    "template <>",
    "struct IsInteger<int> {",
    "    static constexpr bool value = true;",
    "};",
    "",
    "template <typename T>",
    "typename std::enable_if<IsInteger<T>::value, void>::type",
    "process(T t) {",
    "    std::cout << t << \" is an integer type.\" << std::endl;",
    "}",
    "",
    "template <typename T>",
    "typename std::enable_if<!IsInteger<T>::value, void>::type",
    "process(T t) {",
    "    std::cout << t << \" is not an integer type.\" << std::endl;",
    "}",
    "",
    "int main() {",
    "    process(42);        // Calls the integer version",
    "    process(3.14);      // Calls the non-integer version",
    "    process(\"hello\"); // Calls the non-integer version",
    "    return 0;",
    "}"
